        },
        "result": "I've implemented all three services and re-routed the gateway. I couldn't build any of it, because `mvn` isn't installed in this workspace, so none of the code has been compiled or run.\n\n**What each service does**\n- **market-service:** `GET /api/quotes/{symbol}` returns `{symbol, price}` from the fixed catalog and answers 400 for an unknown symbol.\n- **user-service:**\n  - `POST /api/users` creates a user with 10000.00 cash and returns 201, or 400 for a duplicate or blank username.\n  - `GET /api/users/{id}/portfolio` returns `cash`, `cashBalance`, `holdings` and `totalValue`. It fetches prices from market-service through Eureka.\n  - `GET /api/users/{id}` is an internal lookup used by trade-service.\n  - `POST /internal/users/{id}/apply` applies a buy or sell in one local transaction, with a row lock on the user.\n    - It returns 404 for an unknown user.\n    - It returns 400 for insufficient cash or position.\n    - A rejected apply changes nothing.\n- **trade-service:**\n  - `POST /api/trades/buy` and `/sell` check shares, then symbol (market-service), then call the user-service apply endpoint.\n  - Only after user-service accepts does it save the trade record and return 201.\n  - It then publishes the trade to `financial.exchange` with key `trade.completed`, bound to `trade.audit.queue`. A RabbitMQ failure is logged and does not fail the trade.\n  - `GET /api/users/{id}/trades` checks the user exists (404 if not) and returns the history, each item with `type` BUY or SELL.\n- **api-gateway:** I edited `application.yml` only. `/api/users/*/trades` goes to trade-service, and the other `/api/users` paths (including portfolio) go to user-service. `/api/quotes/**` and `/api/trades/**` route as before. `docker-compose.yml` is untouched.\n\n**Uncertainty**\n- **Check order:** when a request has several problems, the order is shares, then symbol, then user. A request with an invalid symbol and an unknown user therefore returns 400, not 404. The contract doesn't say which should win.\n- **Half-applied trade:** if trade-service crashes after user-service applies a trade but before it saves the record, the two states diverge. That follows from the no-distributed-transaction rule.\n- **Maven versions:** compatibility with the Spring Boot 3.5.0 / Spring Cloud 2025.0.0 setup is unchecked, since nothing was built. The code uses a load-balanced `RestClient` rather than Feign.",
