        "result": "I found a likely cause in the gateway config and fixed it, but I haven't started or tested anything, so it's unconfirmed. The evidence you sent shows user-service and trade-service starting normally, with RabbitMQ up, and nothing from api-gateway.\n\nMy earlier route rewrite of `api-gateway/src/main/resources/application.yml` split the file at the wrong `server:` line. It matched the indented `server:` under `spring.cloud.gateway`. That left a stray duplicate `server:` block with partial route definitions in the middle of the file. That malformed YAML would stop the gateway from starting.\n\nI rewrote the file so it has one clean route list and the original `server`, `eureka` and `management` sections:\n- `/api/users/*/trades` goes to trade-service.\n- `/api/users` and `/api/users/**` go to user-service.\n- `/api/quotes/**` goes to market-service.\n- `/api/trades/**` goes to trade-service.\n\nI changed no Java code and didn't touch the Compose topology.",
